---
// The proposals index (formerly proposals/index.html), restyled. Words unchanged; the advisory footer line is dropped.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const substack = "https://inixiative.substack.com";
---
<Base
  title="Governance: designs for cooperation at scale · inixiative"
  description="Designs for cooperation at scale, published to be argued with. Multi-scale governance, the energy standard and the platform, with the whitepaper research behind them."
  domain="governance"
  current="governance"
  light
  canonical="/governance/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span>Governance</span>
    <h1 class="display-1">Designs for cooperation at scale, <span class="accent">published to be argued with</span>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Every institution we live under was designed, most of them long ago, for a different
      world and without an off switch. These proposals are attempts at better ones. Each states what it's for,
      how it works, who it pays and how, and where it could break. If a design can't survive being attacked
      in public, it doesn't deserve to govern anyone.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="proposals-title">
    <h2 id="proposals-title" class="eyebrow" data-quiet>The proposals</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <a class="card" href="/proposals/governance/">
        <div class="card-head"><span class="eyebrow">Proposal 01</span><span class="tag">draft · part one</span></div>
        <h3>Multi-scale governance</h3>
        <p>How a society decides. Proposing, deciding, and repealing law split across three tiers; lawmakers paid for
          how long their work survives; every institution built with a lifecycle: spun up, held accountable, and
          sunset when its work is done.</p>
        <p class="meta">Read the proposal →</p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href={`${substack}/p/the-energy-standard`}>
        <div class="card-head"><span class="eyebrow">Proposal 02</span><span class="tag">part two</span></div>
        <h3>The energy standard</h3>
        <p>How a society settles up. A currency backed by energy, minted when a kilowatt-hour is produced and burned
          when it's consumed, so the money supply grows with real productive capacity instead of political
          convenience.</p>
        <p class="meta">Read on Substack →</p>
      </a>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-head"><span class="eyebrow">Proposal 03</span><span class="tag">research</span></div>
        <h3>The platform</h3>
        <p>How a society stores value. A marketplace for real-world assets where every price is proven at auction and
          every token is created for cash at its backing. A timeline shows how value moves between every party.</p>
        <div class="card-links">
          <a class="text-link" href="/proposals/platform/">The platform</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/proposals/platform/timeline/">The timeline</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section anchor-target" id="planned" aria-labelledby="planned-title">
    <div class="card" data-raised>
      <div class="card-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Planned</span>
        <span class="tag" data-tone="progress">Planned · nothing built for users yet</span>
      </div>
      <h2 id="planned-title" class="display-3">The Inixiative project</h2>
      <p>
        A platform where a group pools money, tracks who owns what with tokens, and releases funds only when
        the participants agree a milestone was met. Each initiative governs itself: the marketplace it runs in
        can't change its rules, move its funds or override its votes.
      </p>
      <p>
        It started as governance software. A friend pointed me to managing money as the practical place to
        start, because it forces real cooperation. The first use case is cattle trusts in Uruguay and
        Argentina. It will be built on template, the SaaS app I've been building from the building blocks.
      </p>
      <div class="card-links">
        <a class="text-link" href="/proposals/platform/">The write-up: a marketplace for real-world assets</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <article class="prose">
      <span class="eyebrow" data-quiet>The research behind them</span>
      <p>Behind these proposals sits the <a
          href="https://github.com/inixiative/whitepaper">whitepaper</a>, a young working document that is still
        changing. It tries to explain the moment we're in and civilization in general: why governance fails, what any
        replacement must accomplish, and which mechanisms have only just become possible. Among them: voting that
        captures what people want, pay that ties leaders to the long term, and checks that keep power
        honest without trusting anyone to stay virtuous. Each proposal assembles some of those mechanisms into
        one design. There are many possible assemblies; these are the ones we think are worth arguing about
        first.</p>
      <p>Terms used across the proposals and the code are defined in the <a href="/vocabulary/">vocabulary</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="follow">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Argue with these.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Every proposal lists its own attack surfaces, because we want them attacked. Follow the work as it develops,
          or come take a swing.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="mailto:aron.greenspan@inixiative.com?subject=On%20the%20proposals">Tell us where they break</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/moving-forward/">Moving forward</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <iframe class="substack" title="Subscribe on Substack" src={`${substack}/embed`} width="480" height="150" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
